# The eval set is hashed byte-for-byte in evals/manifest.json and checked before
# every scoring run. Line-ending conversion would rewrite those bytes on checkout
# and every hash would fail on a fresh clone, so git must leave them alone.
evals/** -text

# A shell script goes to a Linux droplet and runs there. `core.autocrlf=true` on
# this machine checks one out CRLF, and a CRLF script fails at the shebang --
# `/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter` -- which for `trunk_watch.sh` presents as
# nothing happening and the wsd trunk being unrecoverable after iter 183,106.
# The blobs are already LF; this stops the checkout from undoing that.
*.sh -text

# The v4 run artefacts are hashed in their own RUN-NOTES; a CRLF checkout
# would silently break every recorded sha256, same class as the trunk_watch.sh
# footgun fixed 2026-08-29.
/260M?Run?Data?v4/* -text

# Theme art. Git detects PNG as binary on its own, so this is belt-and-braces
# against a future `*.json`-adjacent rule or an autocrlf setting reaching it --
# same class as the three above, and a sprite sheet mangled on checkout would
# present as a face that renders as nothing.
*.png binary

# The studio page's vendored libraries are held to the sha256 recorded in
# harness/studio/web/vendor/README.md by scripts/check_studio.py. A CRLF
# checkout would rewrite those bytes on every fresh Windows clone and fail
# the sweep there -- the eval-set and run-artefact class again.
harness/studio/web/vendor/*.js -text
